<title>USA: FMR group corrects stake size in Vimpel.</title>
<headline>FMR group corrects stake size in Vimpel.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by FMR Corp said Thursday its stake in Vimpel-Communications (Open Joint Stock Co) should be 1.31 percent or 304,160 American Depositary Receipts not 5.8 percent as declared on January 28.</p>
<p>The initial stake was filed in error, FMR said in the filing.</p>
<p>FMR Corp is the parent to Fidelity Management &amp; Research Co, investment adviser to Fidelity Funds.</p>
<p>The Moscow-based mobile telephone firm first began trading on November 14, 1996 as the first Russian company to trade on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
